From: EglantinePS5
Subject: up: EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_WHY totals from a timer thread too (EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_WHY_EVERY_S, 10 s), not only from TickFrame

Why: in test d4 the WHY totals printed from PipelineCache::TickFrame only (every 60 frames, at most
once a minute through LogShaderSetAudit). The frames stalled after about 387 s and the start died
at 555 s without a shutdown line, so the count stopped at 43 of the 611 pipelines the start asked
for. Between 130 and 311 s the totals were also skipped because "asked" had not moved, though the
catalogue had become ready and the waiting samples had been sorted.

What (only with EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_WHY=1, which needs EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET=1): StartShaderSet starts a
small thread that every EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_WHY_EVERY_S seconds (default 10, 1-3600) sorts the
waiting samples and prints the totals line when a count moved (a new ask, or samples resolved since
the last line). The GPU thread's NoteShaderSetWhy and every drain now hold set_why_mutex, so the
timer and the GPU thread never touch the counts at once. TickFrame's line every 60 s and the
shutdown line stay; the destructor stops the timer before the shutdown line. A crash loses at most
the last interval's counts.

Off (EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_WHY unset): no thread, no lock taken (NoteShaderSetWhy is not called).
On: one uncontended lock per new graphics pipeline.

Test: with EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_WHY=1 the "EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_WHY totals" line appears within about
10 s of each change, also while frames stall; the last line before a crash has asked close to the
first_start.list's G + M rows.
